The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
ctx = blk_mq_get_ctx(q);
hctx = blk_mq_map_queue(q, ctx->cpu);
data->hctx = hctx;
```
Reason:
The bug occurs when the system sleeps due to running out of requests, which can cause `blk_mq_get_ctx(q)` to return a stale context. As a result, `hctx` and `ctx` may point to outdated structures, leading to `data->hctx` being set to an incorrect value. This can corrupt `ctx->rq_list` when new requests are inserted, as the wrong lock may be used.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
data->hctx = alloc_data.hctx;
data->ctx = alloc_data.ctx;
hctx->queued++;
```
Reason:
The fix updates `data->hctx` and `data->ctx` to use the values from `alloc_data`, which are guaranteed to be current and valid. This ensures that the correct context is used when inserting requests, preventing corruption of `ctx->rq_list` and ensuring that the right lock is acquired.

